s potential patterns like All Simples if J2 is discarded later, but currently, safety is prioritized given the aggressive play of opponents with multiple Pungs. Discarding T4 maintains the pairs (T7 and B6) for flexibility in forming Pungs or keeping as the final pair.  \n\nAnswer: Play T4"}
